"John H." <JohnWH@gmail.com> writes:

> In my opinion, the potion and spell of restore ability are victims of
> Nethack's tendency towards powergaming.  There is no thing they provide
> over unicorn horns that can't be made up for simply by being careful of
> curses and possibly using a couple extra turns, AND uncorn horns do
> other cool things besides: they can be used as quite a good weapon,
> they can cure most ill effects including hallucination, and they can
> even turn some potions into water or fruit juice, which is also an
> identification aid.

The potion is marginally useful because it may turn up before a
unicorn horn.  One identified potion of restore ability won't let you
keep eating poisonous corpses, but it will let you quaff-identify a
potion that might be sickness.

I have never had any use for the spell, and certainly it is pointless
as a crowning gift, since by then you're bound to have a unicorn horn.
